{'id': '2608.01772', 'categories': ['cs.AI'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.01772', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01772', 'authors': ['Xuhui Wang', 'Ruoqi Shu', 'Chen Dan', 'Tianhua Xu', 'Mengxi Luo', 'Yanming Mai', 'Bo Wan'], 'title': 'FRAMES: Guarded and Dual-Objective Skill Evolution for Agents in Policy-Governed Enterprise Workflows', 'comment': None, 'summary': 'LLM agents increasingly run policy-bound enterprise workflows such as document auditing, where they must apply rules consistently, ground every value, and stay auditable. Improving these agents is hard: operational feedback is sparse and unlabeled, edits to one rule can regress unrelated cases, and accuracy must improve without inflating inference cost or losing auditability. We present FRAMES, a closed-loop framework that cold-starts deployable skills from existing assets and then evolves them through consensus-based mutation, Pareto selection over accuracy and cost, and an anti-regression guarantee, all while preserving auditability. Deployed on our internal production system, FRAMES attains the best accuracy-cost trade-off among baselines, with the same gains reproduced on tau-bench.'}
